WEBVTT

00:08.809 --> 00:10.276
Legend has it that...

00:11.445 --> 00:14.243
...during the Heian Period, there were
men who fought with no weapons...

00:14.581 --> 00:19.917
They were known as the Men of
Carnage and they reigned undefeated.

00:21.388 --> 00:26.553
Their technique was called
the Mutsu Enmei Style.

00:39.673 --> 00:47.102
<i>The Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

00:47.380 --> 00:53.216
<i>Rushing through my innocent</i>
<i>youth without a care in the world.</i>

00:54.755 --> 01:00.660
<i>This soul of mine is</i>
<i>so easy to influence.</i>

01:02.329 --> 01:06.095
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

01:06.199 --> 01:09.396
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

01:13.173 --> 01:20.238
<i>This is what I'm wishing</i>
<i>for as I sing this song.</i>

01:20.413 --> 01:26.249
<i>I want you to acknowledge</i>
<i>me, that's all.</i>

01:27.120 --> 01:34.390
<i>You smiled at me for</i>
<i>the very first time.</i>

01:34.561 --> 01:42.969
<i>Thank you so much, thank you</i>
<i>from the bottom of my heart.</i>

01:43.670 --> 01:45.331
<i>I'll never forget it.</i>

01:55.081 --> 01:58.517
<i>The Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

02:00.420 --> 02:06.222
<i>The Year 1853</i>

02:16.336 --> 02:19.669
Commodore Perry, commander
of the East India Squadron...

02:19.773 --> 02:23.903
...has sailed into Uraga
Harbor leading four battleships.

02:24.211 --> 02:26.771
These came to be known as the
Kurofune.

02:28.048 --> 02:31.381
From this moment on, the nation
would be catapulted into a...

02:31.484 --> 02:31.785
<i>One Year Later</i>

02:31.785 --> 02:34.913
Tempestuous era called the Bakumatsu.
<i>One Year Later</i>

02:37.791 --> 02:39.053
What are we going to do?

02:39.192 --> 02:41.387
Do you think we're going to
have to fight the foreigners?

02:41.528 --> 02:43.018
Don't be so spineless!

02:43.330 --> 02:46.265
Even if we go to war,
our Bakufu is sure to win!

02:46.733 --> 02:47.427
Huh?

02:48.034 --> 02:48.830
Hey!

02:49.336 --> 02:52.533
Man, what a sight!

02:52.873 --> 02:55.137
Hey, don't just hang back there.

02:55.342 --> 02:57.242
Come on over here and
have a look yourselves!

02:57.410 --> 02:58.672
Who the hell are you?

02:58.778 --> 02:59.972
How'd you get over here?

03:00.080 --> 03:02.708
Cha, cha, cha! This is amazing.

03:03.183 --> 03:04.912
So that's the Kurofune?

03:05.018 --> 03:09.079
I'd love to have just one of
those ships to call my own!

03:11.091 --> 03:15.255
There was someone who gazed at the
Kurofune with a different perspective...

03:15.362 --> 03:18.263
...this young man standing here...

03:19.966 --> 03:23.163
<i>Four Years Later</i>

03:30.176 --> 03:30.904
Hmm...

03:35.181 --> 03:36.375
Match point!

03:36.816 --> 03:37.942
Stop!

03:38.718 --> 03:40.481
Cha, cha, cha!

03:40.987 --> 03:43.114
What do you know, I won!

03:43.390 --> 03:45.654
He lost? Komanosuke
Shimada, of all people?

03:45.792 --> 03:47.783
This is the first time I've ever seen...

03:47.894 --> 03:50.761
...Shimada lose a match since
switching to the two-sword technique!

03:51.197 --> 03:53.757
Listen, who is that man?

03:53.900 --> 03:57.666
Sir! He is the Head Instructor of the
Kochiba Dojo's Hokushin Itto-Style...

03:57.904 --> 03:59.929
...and one of our own
Tosa Domain goshi.

04:02.342 --> 04:04.310
Oh, so he's nothing but a goshi...

04:04.411 --> 04:06.879
Hey, nice going, Ryoma!
That was masterful!

04:07.013 --> 04:08.878
Who knew you'd end up
beating that Shimada!

04:09.316 --> 04:11.944
Cha, cha, cha! It was just dumb luck!

04:14.154 --> 04:14.950
Begin!

04:15.555 --> 04:18.524
With Perry's arrival, Japan now
felt threatened by foreign nations.

04:18.658 --> 04:22.424
Literature had been valued over martial
arts, but now this trend was reversed.

04:22.662 --> 04:26.120
Through the good offices of Youdou
Yamanouchi, leader of the Tosa Area...

04:26.466 --> 04:29.867
104 swordsmen have
been invited to compete...

04:30.003 --> 04:33.370
...in a tournament at
the Tosa residence in Edo.

04:33.540 --> 04:34.905
I concede...

04:36.109 --> 04:38.373
So now it's a showdown
between Chiba and Saitoh!

04:38.712 --> 04:41.442
All right, your next
opponent is Katsura of Choshu.

04:41.548 --> 04:43.448
Show him the Tosa spirit, now!

04:43.850 --> 04:46.182
Easier said than done, Takechi.

04:46.453 --> 04:50.583
Sure, Katsura's a great swordsman
and he's renowned all over Edo.

04:50.757 --> 04:53.248
But still I know you
can beat him, Ryoma.

04:53.360 --> 04:55.828
Just show him the underlying
strength of the Chiba School!

04:56.196 --> 04:59.427
The Tosa spirit and the underlying
strength of the Chiba School?

04:59.566 --> 05:01.625
Maybe you two should
be competing instead!

05:03.603 --> 05:06.834
Well, I have my duties
as an official attendant...

05:07.140 --> 05:09.904
And I'm still getting over that bruise
I took in practice the other day...

05:10.276 --> 05:12.073
I hear you, I hear you.

05:12.479 --> 05:16.108
People have high hopes for you two.
You shouldn't be competing here.

05:16.449 --> 05:17.848
Me, on the other hand...

05:17.951 --> 05:21.250
...it's a wonder a fool like me
even got to be Head Instructor!

05:21.354 --> 05:23.686
So even if I lose, it's no big deal.

05:23.823 --> 05:26.189
Hokushin Itto Style,
Lord Ryoma Sakamoto...

05:26.292 --> 05:27.623
Report for your match!

05:27.727 --> 05:29.627
Gotta go now. See you later!

05:33.533 --> 05:35.467
That Ryoma...

05:35.568 --> 05:37.866
Doesn't he ever get
the least bit nervous?

05:38.004 --> 05:40.939
Well, that's part of what
makes him a great swordsman.

05:41.574 --> 05:42.905
All right, then...

05:45.145 --> 05:46.043
Bow!

05:47.213 --> 05:49.909
Mr. Katsura, I hope you go easy on me.

05:50.116 --> 05:53.517
Sakamoto, since we've bowed to each
other, that means the match has begun.

05:53.653 --> 05:55.883
This is no time for idle chatter!

05:57.357 --> 06:01.123
The Shintoh Munen Style's Saitoh Dojo
Head Instructor, Kogoro Katsura...

06:01.194 --> 06:04.493
...versus the Hokushin Itto Style's
Kochiba Dojo Head Instructor, huh?

06:04.764 --> 06:06.561
Who do you think will win?

06:06.666 --> 06:08.964
That Kochiba Head Instructor
has great talent...

06:09.069 --> 06:11.435
...but there's no way he can
keep up with Katsura's speed.

06:11.604 --> 06:13.799
It'll be Kochiba who wins this match.

06:14.074 --> 06:15.974
Hey, excuse me, guys.

06:16.543 --> 06:19.706
Hey, just as I thought... the
view's better up here!

06:20.246 --> 06:21.213
Hey, you!

06:21.347 --> 06:22.678
He can kick butt!

06:23.316 --> 06:25.147
That Sakamoto fellow, I mean.

06:26.086 --> 06:27.951
Just watch him, now.

06:28.688 --> 06:29.586
Begin!

06:37.997 --> 06:39.123
So quick!

06:39.499 --> 06:41.228
But he's surviving every blow!

06:44.204 --> 06:45.762
Katsura's in top form!

06:45.905 --> 06:46.530
Ryoma!

06:51.978 --> 06:53.502
Can't get a hit!

06:58.551 --> 07:01.486
Hey not bad, not bad!

07:12.332 --> 07:15.062
What the hell? He's
leaving his chest wide open.

07:15.268 --> 07:16.860
Is he challenging me?

07:19.672 --> 07:21.003
The one-handed jodan stance?

07:21.141 --> 07:23.632
Katsura won't be attacking again.

07:23.743 --> 07:25.335
Oh, Joukichi Sensei!

07:25.445 --> 07:26.104
Father...

07:26.513 --> 07:29.073
Looks like he's at
least half-serious now...

07:40.026 --> 07:40.685
Here we go!

07:51.004 --> 07:52.995
What kind of attack is this?

07:53.373 --> 07:54.840
It's just like...

07:55.875 --> 07:57.308
It's just like...

08:12.759 --> 08:14.249
A tsunami!

08:14.861 --> 08:16.726
Match point! Stop.

08:18.398 --> 08:19.296
He did it!

08:19.399 --> 08:20.331
Ryoma!

08:28.341 --> 08:31.071
That's just the tip of
the iceberg, isn't it?

08:32.879 --> 08:34.574
Hey, I'm pretty tired now!

08:37.951 --> 08:43.412
<i>One Year Later</i>

08:48.595 --> 08:52.053
<i>Chiba Dojo</i>

08:54.934 --> 08:56.265
Brother?

08:57.470 --> 08:58.630
What is it, Sanako?

08:58.771 --> 09:01.706
If you've come to see Ryoma,
he's not here right now.

09:02.242 --> 09:05.803
What makes you think I'd come
here just to see Lord Sakamoto?

09:07.680 --> 09:08.612
So?

09:08.815 --> 09:11.784
I wanted to tell you that a
friend of Lord Sakamoto's is here.

09:12.218 --> 09:13.082
Really?

09:13.186 --> 09:15.984
In that case, show him
in and have him wait.

09:16.789 --> 09:17.483
What's the matter?

09:17.590 --> 09:20.218
The thing is, I was about
to take him to the parlor...

09:20.326 --> 09:23.818
...but he said, "I'm hungry,
where's the kitchen?"

09:24.197 --> 09:25.186
What?

09:25.632 --> 09:28.260
What's this about the kitchen?

09:29.869 --> 09:33.703
I see, so did you show him the
way to the kitchen, Miss Sanako?

09:33.806 --> 09:34.932
No, I didn't!

09:35.708 --> 09:38.302
He must have a keen sense of
smell, he found the way himself.

09:38.745 --> 09:41.873
So what's this guy doing right now?

09:43.316 --> 09:44.180
Aha, I see.

09:49.989 --> 09:51.251
Lord Sakamoto?

09:52.225 --> 09:53.522
Miss Sanako.

09:53.793 --> 09:54.657
Yes!

09:56.195 --> 09:57.753
I'd like to eat now, too!

09:58.798 --> 09:59.321
Oh...

10:07.240 --> 10:08.798
Miss Sanako, another helping!

10:08.908 --> 10:09.567
Yes.

10:09.676 --> 10:10.506
Me, too.

10:11.177 --> 10:12.940
You're still not satisfied?

10:14.180 --> 10:14.908
Here.

10:17.517 --> 10:20.452
Brother, is this the
Tosa way of doing things?

10:20.620 --> 10:24.351
Sitting down to eat with your
guest as soon as he arrives?

10:25.391 --> 10:29.350
Say, Ryoma, if you don't mind, how
about introducing us to your friend?

10:29.862 --> 10:31.329
I have no idea who he is!

10:31.631 --> 10:32.393
Huh?

10:32.632 --> 10:33.792
Then he's not your...

10:36.035 --> 10:37.332
Thanks for the meal.

10:37.403 --> 10:38.267
Man!

10:38.571 --> 10:40.232
I'm stuffed now!

10:40.640 --> 10:42.198
Who the hell are you, anyway?

10:42.375 --> 10:44.935
Hey, Sakamoto, you're a great
swordsman.

10:45.345 --> 10:47.336
I saw your match in the
Shogun's Tournament last year.

10:47.447 --> 10:49.415
Hey, you! I'm talking to you!

10:49.682 --> 10:53.174
Since then, I've visited
dojos all over the country...

10:53.353 --> 10:55.753
...but I've never found
anyone of your caliber.

10:55.855 --> 10:57.345
That's not what I'm asking you!

10:57.657 --> 11:00.251
Cha, cha, cha! You're
embarrassing me now!

11:01.094 --> 11:03.153
But you weren't going for the kill.

11:03.563 --> 11:06.361
I know that wasn't anywhere
near your best stuff...

11:06.899 --> 11:09.459
Oh, you don't think so?

11:10.002 --> 11:13.165
I'd like to make you go for the kill...

11:17.110 --> 11:19.237
Is that your way of challenging him?

11:19.345 --> 11:21.279
Well, I guess it is, actually.

11:21.647 --> 11:23.808
You want to make me go for the kill?

11:23.950 --> 11:27.010
You came all the way to the
prestigious Chiba Dojo to do that?

11:27.153 --> 11:28.711
Ryoma, there's no
need for you to accept.

11:28.821 --> 11:30.448
We can just have one of
our students take him on...

11:30.590 --> 11:32.148
Not a good idea.

11:33.025 --> 11:36.051
Not only did he show up alone at one
of the three biggest dojos in Japan...

11:36.195 --> 11:38.789
...to challenge me, but he's
also helped himself to your food!

11:39.065 --> 11:41.829
That takes guts and
the skill to back it up!

11:42.902 --> 11:46.998
Hey, who knew there were such
oddball characters in the world!

11:47.106 --> 11:48.038
This is great!

11:49.375 --> 11:53.368
Actually, if you're eating
lunch with someone like him...

11:53.513 --> 11:55.504
...you're pretty odd yourself!

11:55.915 --> 11:57.348
Hey, forgot to ask.

11:57.483 --> 11:59.212
What's your name?

11:59.318 --> 12:00.512
Who, me?

12:00.753 --> 12:02.846
Izumi Mutsu!

12:03.256 --> 12:05.816
I'm Ryoma Sakamoto.

12:06.926 --> 12:13.024
<i>Slumbering Dragon</i>

12:18.805 --> 12:19.464
Next!

12:19.572 --> 12:19.806
<i>A Few Days Later</i>

12:19.806 --> 12:20.973
Please!
<i>A Few Days Later</i>

12:20.973 --> 12:27.606
<i>A Few Days Later</i>

12:29.582 --> 12:30.606
Next!

12:30.817 --> 12:31.579
Yes!

12:34.921 --> 12:36.115
Please!

12:46.265 --> 12:46.959
Next!

12:48.301 --> 12:49.598
Please!

12:58.478 --> 13:01.777
What's wrong? You've been
pretty merciless lately, Sanako.

13:02.348 --> 13:04.009
That's not true.

13:04.183 --> 13:06.651
I'm just training as hard as I can.

13:06.786 --> 13:08.515
Since I'm not like Lord Sakamoto!

13:09.522 --> 13:12.218
Just as I thought,
Ryoma's the cause of this...

13:12.325 --> 13:13.485
I have an idea.

13:13.593 --> 13:16.494
Brother, why don't you have
a word with Lord Sakamoto?

13:16.963 --> 13:19.090
Shirking practice day after day...

13:19.198 --> 13:21.860
...all he does is fool
around with that strange man!

13:22.001 --> 13:24.834
The other day, he spent
the whole afternoon...

13:25.071 --> 13:27.835
...staring up at the
clouds by the river!

13:35.748 --> 13:37.477
Too much free time...

13:37.783 --> 13:38.943
You see?

13:41.387 --> 13:43.548
No, I'm talking about you.

13:44.657 --> 13:48.184
You followed them, and secretly
watched them the whole time, right?

13:49.662 --> 13:52.495
Oh, since that strange
man stole Ryoma away...

13:52.598 --> 13:56.125
...he won't give you the time
of day, so you're jealous, right?

13:58.538 --> 13:59.596
No, you're wrong!

13:59.739 --> 14:01.730
This is not about me at all!

14:02.241 --> 14:04.334
The thing is, that Mutsu fellow said...

14:04.443 --> 14:07.105
...he came here to
challenge Lord Sakamoto...

14:07.246 --> 14:09.339
...yet he hasn't raised a
finger since the day he got here!

14:09.549 --> 14:12.313
On the contrary, he's a freeloader
who's wormed his way into our house.

14:12.418 --> 14:15.080
...the one thing he does do
is eat more than anyone else!

14:15.421 --> 14:17.321
He's just waiting, that's all.

14:17.990 --> 14:18.718
Father!

14:19.225 --> 14:23.184
He's waiting, see. For
Ryoma to get motivated.

14:23.796 --> 14:27.892
Are you saying that Ryoma doesn't
yet have that motivation, Father?

14:28.200 --> 14:31.192
Ryoma is what you'd call
a genius with the sword.

14:31.337 --> 14:36.707
But he does have a fault.
That is, he's far too gentle.

14:36.809 --> 14:40.836
Granted, he smashed Katsura's
bokuto in the Shogun's Tournament...

14:40.947 --> 14:43.677
but then he stopped within
an inch of cracking his skull!

14:45.651 --> 14:48.643
That in itself was an
astounding feat, but...

14:48.788 --> 14:51.416
...I think it shows that
Ryoma is incapable of killing.

14:53.426 --> 14:55.724
Too gentle, you say?

14:56.762 --> 15:00.198
That is what prevents
Ryoma's sword from awakening.

15:00.466 --> 15:04.300
Do you mean that
man has the power to awaken him?

15:04.470 --> 15:06.267
I find that hard to believe, too!

15:08.274 --> 15:12.506
Do you know where that
fellow sleeps every night?

15:12.612 --> 15:13.306
Huh?

15:15.948 --> 15:19.179
How many men would
come here to fight...

15:19.285 --> 15:23.221
...yet be brazen enough to sleep
with abandon in the Chiba Dojo?

15:23.723 --> 15:27.523
Not only that, but he refuses
to hide in enemy territory...

15:27.627 --> 15:30.653
It takes more nerve than most of
us are endowed with to do that...

15:30.796 --> 15:34.926
That's the kind of man who can walk
through hell with a smile on his face...

15:35.568 --> 15:40.767
Or perhaps I should say, he's
like a Ryoma Sakamoto who can kill.

15:40.873 --> 15:44.536
That's probably why Ryoma's
taking such a liking to him.

15:46.345 --> 15:49.974
He just doesn't seem to
be the man you say he is.

15:50.116 --> 15:51.845
Not to me, either.

15:52.018 --> 15:53.315
So you don't see it?

15:53.452 --> 15:56.910
Well, I'm telling you, that
man is undeniably powerful...

15:57.023 --> 15:57.512
Hmm...

15:57.957 --> 16:01.188
If he's a Mutsu from that
legendary clan of Mutsus...

16:01.327 --> 16:04.023
...then he's beyond powerful...

16:04.130 --> 16:04.994
We'll see...

16:08.034 --> 16:09.160
I'm home!

16:09.268 --> 16:10.963
Man, I'm starving!

16:12.438 --> 16:14.633
Me too, I could eat a horse!

16:14.974 --> 16:16.305
Lord Sakamoto?

16:16.642 --> 16:18.667
May I have a word with you?

16:19.412 --> 16:20.436
What is it?

16:20.613 --> 16:22.342
Hey, is dinner ready yet?

16:24.383 --> 16:25.941
How should I know?

16:26.519 --> 16:28.453
I can see you don't like me...

16:31.123 --> 16:34.684
Lord Sakamoto, may I ask you
something?

16:34.827 --> 16:35.851
Sure.

16:36.228 --> 16:39.755
Why are you spending so
much time with Lord Mutsu?

16:39.899 --> 16:42.800
I don't believe it's in your
best interests, Lord Sakamoto!

16:43.235 --> 16:44.497
Well...

16:49.075 --> 16:51.942
I really like the sea, you know!

16:52.778 --> 16:54.040
Yes, I know that.

16:54.146 --> 16:56.341
What does that have to do with it?

16:56.682 --> 16:59.173
You see, I used to go down
to Katsurahama in Tosa...

16:59.318 --> 17:01.377
...and just stand there looking at it...

17:01.487 --> 17:02.215
Yes...

17:02.655 --> 17:06.591
The sea is something that
can blow your mind, you know!

17:08.828 --> 17:11.126
I-Is it, really?

17:11.497 --> 17:14.591
You wouldn't know, because you've
only seen the rivers in Edo.

17:15.034 --> 17:17.229
The sea has an amazing power!

17:17.369 --> 17:20.361
Because normally it's
just a vast body of water...

17:20.539 --> 17:23.474
...but once a storm strikes,
it makes your whole body shiver!

17:23.776 --> 17:26.540
All right, but what does that
have to do with my question?

17:27.012 --> 17:30.709
Well, I'm telling you,
Izumi's just like the sea...

17:30.916 --> 17:31.780
Huh?

17:54.106 --> 17:55.801
You wish to speak to me?

17:56.008 --> 17:59.535
You're distracting me. Would you
mind not staring at me like that?

18:00.346 --> 18:02.746
So intense this early in the morning...

18:02.948 --> 18:05.109
The dojo's closed today, isn't it?

18:05.518 --> 18:07.213
I am the daughter of Master Chiba.

18:07.319 --> 18:10.288
There is no day off for one
who wishes to hone one's skills.

18:12.358 --> 18:13.825
It's really too bad.

18:13.959 --> 18:15.153
What is?

18:15.294 --> 18:17.728
That you've already fallen for Ryoma!

18:19.765 --> 18:21.528
I don't know what you're talking about!

18:21.700 --> 18:24.533
You're a skilled martial
artist, plus you're a babe!

18:24.703 --> 18:29.299
I guess your only faults are that you're
too jealous, and a little too stubborn...

18:31.143 --> 18:33.475
What is he saying? This strange man!

18:33.579 --> 18:35.911
Oh, Miss Sanako! I've
been looking for you!

18:36.282 --> 18:38.079
Oh, Lord Sakamoto!

18:38.350 --> 18:41.342
Izumi's here too? Perfect!

18:41.687 --> 18:43.484
Since it's such a nice day today...

18:43.589 --> 18:46.456
I thought I'd go look at the
cherry blossoms with Izumi.

18:47.326 --> 18:49.419
Could you make us some
lunch to take along?

18:50.162 --> 18:51.254
Of course.

18:51.664 --> 18:56.363
If you want to catch him, you'd
better not let him out of your sight!

18:58.037 --> 18:59.197
Is something the matter?

18:59.338 --> 19:02.000
Nope. Miss Sanako's going to join us.

19:02.641 --> 19:03.539
Right?

19:04.376 --> 19:08.039
Um, if you don't mind, Lord Sakamoto...

19:13.686 --> 19:16.587
Man, the weather's amazing!

19:16.922 --> 19:21.325
The best thing to do on a day like this is
relax and watch the cherry blossoms.

19:21.493 --> 19:22.687
Right, Miss Sanako?

19:22.795 --> 19:23.887
What? Oh...

19:23.996 --> 19:25.793
Yes, absolutely!

19:26.899 --> 19:28.423
This man is so strange!

19:28.567 --> 19:32.663
I still can't believe he's as
powerful as Father says...

19:34.340 --> 19:36.570
Huh? What's the matter, Izumi?

19:38.043 --> 19:41.206
I didn't know there was a
kenjutsu dojo in a place like this.

19:42.214 --> 19:43.511
Shieikan?

19:43.649 --> 19:45.742
I heard they're well-trained
for the battlefield...

19:45.851 --> 19:47.318
...but they're no good
when it comes to a shinai.

19:48.420 --> 19:49.444
Who's there?

19:53.025 --> 19:54.356
Well, now...

19:54.460 --> 19:57.554
I thought I'd been to
most of the dojos in Edo...

19:57.663 --> 20:00.962
...but who knew I'd find someone
like you in a dump like this!

20:01.300 --> 20:02.631
Izumi...

20:04.336 --> 20:05.735
Ryoma Sakamoto...

20:06.105 --> 20:10.405
Cha, cha, cha! Hey, how did
you know my name, anyway?

20:10.542 --> 20:12.942
Because ever since the
Shogun's Tournament...

20:13.045 --> 20:15.206
...you have been renowned
as the best swordsman in Edo.

20:15.648 --> 20:20.813
Unfortunately, the Shieikan was not
granted the opportunity to compete...

20:21.186 --> 20:23.620
Well, that really is a shame.

20:23.923 --> 20:27.324
I'll bet you would've advanced
pretty far if you'd taken part...

20:27.593 --> 20:31.495
Don't you dare mock the Shieikan just
because we're not well known!

20:31.797 --> 20:35.790
Cha, cha, cha...
I'm not mocking you at all, see...

20:35.935 --> 20:37.197
Man, that's youth!

20:37.770 --> 20:40.295
Sure, you're young, but you'd
better give this a pass.

20:40.806 --> 20:41.898
What?

20:42.441 --> 20:43.567
Gifted...

20:44.510 --> 20:47.479
You were born with remarkable talent...

20:47.646 --> 20:52.106
Still, at your current level, you
have no chance against Ryoma or me!

20:58.290 --> 20:59.484
Soushi...

21:00.960 --> 21:04.123
Tennen Rishin Style, Soushi Okita...

21:05.764 --> 21:08.232
If you dare mock me any further...

21:08.434 --> 21:09.423
I'll kill you!

21:10.736 --> 21:13.364
It was a time when, in the
struggle for the dawn of Japan...

21:13.472 --> 21:15.565
...many young men dreamed...

21:15.674 --> 21:19.576
...staked their youth on its
coming, and gave up their lives.

21:19.945 --> 21:24.575
Those who came after called
this era the "Bakumatsu."

21:24.883 --> 21:27.044
<i>To be continued...</i>

21:37.730 --> 21:49.767
<i>Those summer stars, I looked up at</i>
<i>them alone when I was a troubled child.</i>

21:50.042 --> 21:59.781
<i>My loneliness and the vast night</i>
<i>sky, melting and shining in eternity.</i>

21:59.918 --> 22:08.917
<i>I just don't know what this</i>
<i>dream means, if it leads to love...</i>

22:09.061 --> 22:19.733
<i>Even if it's just "hello,"</i>
<i>I want to hear your voice.</i>

22:20.773 --> 22:26.905
<i>The person I am today</i>
<i>is about to disappear...</i>

22:27.279 --> 22:30.271
<i>What is it that will hold me back?</i>

22:31.150 --> 22:37.419
<i>Will it be you? I won't ask you now.</i>

22:37.723 --> 22:43.218
<i>Maybe if we ever meet again...</i>

22:57.976 --> 23:00.638
Ryoma, tell me, do you have a dream?

23:00.846 --> 23:04.543
My dream is to find something more
powerful than the Mutsu Enmei Style.

23:05.584 --> 23:07.484
Next episode of the Age of Chaos...

23:07.786 --> 23:09.413
<i>Patriot of the Sea</i>

23:09.521 --> 23:11.887
Pay close attention, and wait!
